[INTERPRETATION]
AP/GW are the zero-bar atoms at threshold 1/14.  Positive rows do not merely have M>1/14; they have exact bars whose height-margin is a stability radius for local threshold or packet perturbations.
A proof quotient that keeps only M forgets bar count, component length, peak location, and whether the witness is a wide robust interval or a thin near-boundary sliver.

